Team Member: Hailu Tesfaye Seyoum
Project: AI-Powered Content Generation Engine for Small Businesses
Period: October 2026
Role: Logo Design, Website UI/UX Design and Mockup Development
What I Did
Logo and Symbol Design: I independently created an owl symbol featuring an owl reading a book. The owl represents intelligence, knowledge, and creativity, which align with the purpose of our AI-powered content generation project. I explored how the symbol could represent the project’s visual identity.
Website Mockup 1 (Dark Theme): I designed the first AIContentPro website mockup with a dark navy background and purple and blue highlights. The design included a homepage, navigation menu, AI content generator, feature cards, and a recent content section. My goal was to create a modern, technology-focused look.
Website Mockup 2 (Light Theme): I created a second website mockup with a white background, blue buttons, and light-blue interface elements. I aimed to make the website look professional, simple, and easy for small business owners to use.
Website Layout and User Interface: I designed the placement of the navigation bar, homepage content, business information fields, content generation options and dashboard.
Design Comparison and Selection: After creating both mockups, our team compared the designs and chose the white-and-blue version for further development. This design provided a cleaner interface and a more business-focused look.
Team Collaboration: The white-and-blue mockup I created was used as a visual reference for the application's redesign. Semir updated the styling to match the mockup, adding blue buttons, rounded cards, dashboard elements, and a light-blue theme.
Problems and Fixes
Creating a Suitable Project Symbol: I needed a symbol that represented the project’s purpose. I developed the owl design to communicate intelligence, learning and creativity.
Choosing the Website’s Visual Style: The dark-themed mockup looked modern, but the team preferred a cleaner design for small business users. I made the white-and-blue version to offer another choice.
Organising the Website Layout: The website needed to show several features without confusing the user. I separated the content generator, business information fields, and recent content into different sections to improve clarity.
Matching the Design to the Application: We used the chosen mockup to guide the website’s development. I shared the visual design as a reference so the final interface would match what we agreed on.

Decisions
Use the owl symbol as the proposed visual identity for AIContentPro.
Select the white-and-blue mockup as the preferred website design.
Use blue buttons, light backgrounds, rounded cards and clear navigation.
Keep the content generator and dashboard organised so users can easily find the main features.
Use the selected mockup as a reference for the team’s website implementation.
